"""Family `pdiag_effects`: what crosses a module boundary besides plain types.

A library module declares higher-order functions, effectful functions and externs,
measures (with a derived alias), unit-carrying values and a unit-generic function, async
functions, a structured-concurrency worker and mutable module state. Three graph shapes
reach it: the entry imports it directly; the entry imports a middle module that wraps
and re-exports it (two hops, effects widening through the wrappers); and a diamond where
the entry imports both. Each usage snippet exercises one crossing (callback of each
effect kind into an imported HOF, `let pure` callers, partial application of imported
effectful functions, an effectful extern re-exported through a wrapper; measures and
aliases used, combined, redeclared or mismatched in the importer, unit-aware roots on
imported values; async functions awaited/`return!`ed/run in the importer, purity of
async, tasks started from imported workers; mutable state mutated through imported
functions, assigned or read across the boundary) and is checked, run, compiled or
compiled `--native` through the CLI.

Generated by add/pfedge/tools/gen_pdiag_effects.py (fixed seed); expected transcripts and written
files were captured from the reference binary.
"""

